- **F1 stepped motion, fixed.** Share of consecutive frames that are identical (difference < 0.03 on 256x144 grey) in shots longer than 1 s: cut-v4 had 12 shots with > 30 % repeated frames (S001 65 %, S007 82 %, S013 78 %, S042 76 %, S085 76 % ...); cut-v6 has 0 (every one of the 17 listed shots is 0 %). The old "new pictures per second" count (0.3 luma threshold) is now 22.5-23.9 in 14 of the 17; the ones below it (S038 0.6, S126 9.6, S028 12.4) are slow smooth drifts, not steps: their per-frame change is non-zero and even (S038 mean 0.20, first-to-last frame difference 13; S126 0.43 / 22), no repeated frames. S038 (18.7 s) is a very slow drift; judge by eye.
- **F4 totem, fixed.** Mid-frames: S088 (f9815, 06:49), S089 (f9898), S090 (f9976), S091 (f10044) all show the same horned totem with a red eye. S107 (f11499, 07:59.1) is now the empty green tiled room with red cables sprouting from the walls, as the shot list asks; S108 is the red-tube world. The reveal now has something to reveal.
- **F5 costume, mostly fixed.** No suspenders and no bag/diagonal strap in any of the 127 mid-frames; Proog is in the long olive coat over the maroon knit in all of S043-S126, no strap. Emo is plain grey-green throughout.
- The 127 shots each have their own picture; each shot boundary shows a hard cut in the difference trace (0 missing; the old "no cut" joins S027/S056/S070 now also cut). No original pixels: mid-frame correlation against all original frames, max 0.66 (same as cut-v4).

